<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Kansas harvest nearly complete.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Kansas harvest nearly complete.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hot, dry weather over the weekend allowed the Kansas hard red winter wheat harvest to near completion, grain dealers said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm guessing Kansas will be listed as 90 to 95 percent done (in the weekly crop progress report due out Monday afternoon),&quot; a south-central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers said some cutting remained in northwest Kansas.</p>
<p>&quot;The wheat coming off in northwest Kansas is not as good as the stuff in the central part of the state, but it's still good. Central Kansas is really the best by far,&quot; the dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers in Kansas and Oklahoma said local meteorologists were forecasting that the hot, dry weather would last at least through Friday.</p>
